2720.             Ok(sfp) => {
2721.                 if !sfp.get_presence().unwrap_or(false) {
2722.                     continue;
2723.                 }
2724.                 // Backfill DOM/VDM thresholds if the insert-time post came back empty.
2725.                 // The reference posts thresholds gated only on identity readability, at
2726.                 // insert/plug/logical-add (xcvrd.py:359/579/841/869) — never in the DOM
2727.                 // poll — because its threaded boot scan reads the threshold page after the
2728.                 // module has settled. This single-threaded daemon fuses those tasks and runs
2729.                 // `sync_port`'s threshold read during the initial sync, when a just-powered
2730.                 // CMIS module's identity/threshold page can still be unreadable (the Python
2731.                 // decode returns None/{} → `read_threshold_info` None → no row written). A
2732.                 // merely-present admin-up port that is never re-inserted (e.g. a spare
2733.                 // logical port) would then keep an absent TRANSCEIVER_DOM_THRESHOLD forever,
2734.                 // so the full per-port INFO+threshold pipeline
